> I've been thinking that there should be a different symbol for piles
> of items that includes items of different types.  That is, a pile of
> gems would just be *, but a pile of gems and scrolls and gold and etc.
> would be... what?  I'm not sure what the symbol should be... what
> standard ASCII symbols aren't already in use?

The digits 6 through 9, and the comma. That's it. (And the comma
is used on the Rogue level.)

> Has this one been discussed before?  If so, what were the thoughts?

I don't believe it has. I'd be against it; knowing the identity of one
item in a pile (but not the size of that pile or any other items) is
more useful to me than knowing that a pile is larger than one item
(but not the identity of any items in it).

